Z||000007||Darren's 87 coupe||09-22-2001||05:11 PM||||yeah I like that boot a lot.  I might go with that look.  What is that off of?  My real question is, does the short shifter work the same as the longer one?  Mine is stock right now and it does look stupid, but I have heard that the short one is harder to shift for lack of leaverage?  Is it the same feel or not?  i might just leave it long so all of you guys will have shifter envy.||||reg||6
Z||000008||LT1 Chop Top||09-22-2001||06:13 PM||||The short shifter came with the car, the new knob is a MOMO Raptor. It didn't fit exactly, I had to file the inside out a bit to make it fit.  It has a very good feel.  I think Ausfiero sells them now (I know he sells MOMO stuff).<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wheel4_1.jpg"> <BR>The shift knob on my 88 from PepBoys.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gt08_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||qwikgta||09-22-2001||10:34 PM||||I'll address the second question first.  I love the feel of the shifter now.  It is short, i cut it off about a 1/2 inch below the last thread and right at the base.  Then had the two welded together.  I had to cut the bottom 1/4 inch of the shifter off to make it fit.  The boot is off some car from the junkyard, no idea what it was..sorry.  It shifts by flicking your wrist not moving your arm, when i get into my 87 i feel like im driveing a bus with my arm in the air.  I love the feel of the 88.  <BR>  As for the console, it is a cake pan...I cut the ends off and made the hole in the middle, bent the sides down and used velcro to hold it to the carpet, just the hook part.  Painted it to match, vinal will come soon, and put on the boot.  Not sure what brand the cake pan was but I got it at a big chain local here in Virginia Beach.  Im sure you can find one too.  I was not looking for a cake pan when I found this, but i needed a metel that was easy to bend and paint, I was going to make it out of wood but then I saw the cake pan sitting on the self and a measured it and it was the correct size, minus the ends.  <P>Strange but true<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000010||grgoyl86||09-22-2001||10:52 PM||||Here's my shifter in my 4-banger:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P9220002.JPG"> <P>It's four inches from the shift plate to the top of the knob. I had to cut off the bottom of the knob!<P>I love it! Much shorter throw, a little bit more effort, but not bad.||||reg||1
